```
D08 A Linux web-server service account runs shell commands (T1190, T1059.004)
The Tomcat service account should run Java, not bash, id or cat /etc/passwd. Here the account is
looked up by name from the hourly passwd snapshot, so no uid is hard-coded. osquery process events.
Sigma version: detections/sigma/D08-java-spawns-shell.yml
```
index=botsv3 sourcetype=osquery:results name=pack_process-monitoring_proc_events
| spath columns.cmdline output=cmd
| spath columns.uid output=uid
| join type=inner host uid
    [ search index=botsv3 sourcetype="Unix:UserAccounts" user=tomcat* user_id!=0
      | dedup host user_id
      | rename user_id as uid, user as service_account
      | table host uid service_account ]
| where match(cmd, "^\"/bin/(ba)?sh\" \"-c\"")
| stats min(_time) as first_alert count by host service_account
| eval first_alert=strftime(first_alert, "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S")
